272
00:15:22.440 --> 00:15:27.540
But it's so important because, again, when
I got audited from insurance,

273
00:15:27.620 --> 00:15:31.980
I did not know the exact way to include
the treatment plan.

274
00:15:32.140 --> 00:15:34.160
I would just say client is making
progress.

275
00:15:34.600 --> 00:15:38.640
But they want more than just client is
making progress or client is making

276
00:15:38.640 --> 00:15:39.220
minimal progress

277
00:15:39.220 --> 00:15:41.480
or client hasn't made progress.

278
00:15:41.540 --> 00:15:43.480
They want that but they want a
justification.

279
00:15:44.260 --> 00:15:48.480
So make sure that you're justifying the
treatment plan as well.

280
00:15:49.600 --> 00:15:54.320
Show the progress the client is making or
explain any barriers to improvements.

281
00:15:55.080 --> 00:15:58.855
Let's just say a client, again, we'll go
back to the client who's having social

282
00:15:58.855 --> 00:15:59.280
anxiety.

283
00:15:59.280 --> 00:16:05.339
You can say client continues to lack
progress

284
00:16:05.339 --> 00:16:12.057
towards treatment goal of going to social
settings

285
00:16:12.057 --> 00:16:14.560
three days a week.

286
00:16:14.980 --> 00:16:21.277
Will continue to utilize CBT or DBT or
whichever type of modality that you like

287
00:16:21.277 --> 00:16:24.740
to use to help the client get through
that.

288
00:16:24.740 --> 00:16:29.200
And client will continue to come to
sessions or something in that nature.

289
00:16:29.360 --> 00:16:36.200
So they just want to see like what exactly
treatment that you are using for that

290
00:16:36.200 --> 00:16:36.800
client.

291
00:16:38.160 --> 00:16:42.380
Document how the client engaged with and
responded to the interventions.

292
00:16:43.080 --> 00:16:48.591
So if you're using like a SOAP note or DAP
note, that kind of helps you know where to

293
00:16:48.591 --> 00:16:49.360
put things.

294
00:16:49.360 --> 00:16:54.583
But if you're free-forming it, make sure
that you are including how the client is

295
00:16:54.583 --> 00:16:55.920
engaging in sessions

296
00:16:55.920 --> 00:17:00.300
and how they're responding to the
treatment modalities that you are using.

297
00:17:00.960 --> 00:17:02.340
Most people use EMDR.

298
00:17:02.720 --> 00:17:05.180
So did they engage in EMDR?

299
00:17:05.960 --> 00:17:07.160
Did they respond well?

300
00:17:07.260 --> 00:17:09.920
Was it hard for them to connect to the
EMDR?

301
00:17:10.580 --> 00:17:15.040
Were they able to get through all the
points in EMDR?

302
00:17:15.680 --> 00:17:16.440
Things in that nature.

303
00:17:17.780 --> 00:17:22.160
Review and revise your treatment goals
regularly at least 90 days.

304
00:17:22.840 --> 00:17:27.440
And what I tell my team is do 90 days for
Medicaid or Medicaid clients.

305
00:17:28.240 --> 00:17:32.600
And then any other insurance, it could be
