306
00:17:32.960 --> 00:17:37.640
But to be best practice or to make it
easy, we're streamlined for it all.

307
00:17:37.740 --> 00:17:42.632
If you don't take Medicaid, then you can
do 90 days if you ‑‑ I'm sorry, six

308
00:17:42.632 --> 00:17:43.140
months.

309
00:17:43.140 --> 00:17:47.280
If you do take Medicaid, then do every 90
days.

310
00:17:47.980 --> 00:17:52.680
Because regardless, they want you to send
over a 90-day review.

311
00:17:53.300 --> 00:17:58.360
And so you need to make sure that you are
updating the treatment plan or revising

312
00:17:58.360 --> 00:18:02.240
or reviewing it every 90 days with your
client.

313
00:18:02.680 --> 00:18:05.200
So not just you saying, oh, yeah.

314
00:18:05.300 --> 00:18:09.754
No, it should be you and your client going
over the treatment plan, seeing how things

315
00:18:09.754 --> 00:18:11.100
are working out for them.

316
00:18:11.100 --> 00:18:16.423
And that's another best way to see if you
‑‑ like to check in for yourself as their

317
00:18:16.423 --> 00:18:17.120
therapist.

318
00:18:17.760 --> 00:18:23.180
That way you can see how they're feeling
about the sessions, if they see themselves

319
00:18:23.180 --> 00:18:24.220
making the progress.

320
00:18:24.320 --> 00:18:28.080
Because we can see them making progress,
but then they probably don't see it for

321
00:18:28.080 --> 00:18:28.680
themselves.

322
00:18:29.120 --> 00:18:31.900
So it would just be best practice to do it
every 90 days.

323
00:18:32.040 --> 00:18:34.220
But, again, you can do it every six months
too.

324
00:18:35.400 --> 00:18:38.360
Remember your documentation tells the
clinical story.

325
00:18:38.600 --> 00:18:41.600
So make it clear, complete, and
compelling.

326
00:18:42.800 --> 00:18:49.560
So that way if a client is done, like they
graduated with you, but then they come

327
00:18:49.560 --> 00:18:51.980
back and now they need to see another
therapist,

328
00:18:52.760 --> 00:18:58.160
that therapist can follow along from where
you ended or started and ended and then

329
00:18:58.160 --> 00:18:59.380
keep it going from there.

330
00:18:59.500 --> 00:19:02.840
So just make sure everything is
understandable.

331
00:19:02.840 --> 00:19:08.020
It's pretty much like you're creating a
journal for your own client.

332
00:19:08.240 --> 00:19:12.700
So this is their journal that you're
writing for them pretty much.

333
00:19:12.760 --> 00:19:17.300
So just make it so that they can follow
along, you can follow along, and if

334
00:19:17.300 --> 00:19:21.520
somebody else needs to go behind you, they
can follow along with it.

335
00:19:22.700 --> 00:19:29.440
If you are taking Medicaid, and also I
just found out Aetna allows

